      "math_academy_id": "q-110011",
      "knowledge_point_id": "33fca834-0063-5252-832f-5efb4be6e599",
      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying Expressions Using the Properties of Expected Value",
      "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[(2Y-8)^{2}]$ if $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=4$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Expanding out the square inside the expected value, using the properties of the expected value, and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[(2Y-8)^{2}] & =\\text{E}[4{Y}^{2}-32Y+64] \\\\  & =4\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-32\\text{E}[Y]+\\text{E}[64] \\\\  & =4\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-32\\text{E}[Y]+64 \\\\  & =4(4)-32(1)+64 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
