  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14094765",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-122394",
      "knowledge_point_id": "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying a Possible Curve Given Its Arc Length As an Integral",
      "problem": "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?",
      "worked_solution": "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\pi .$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\pi ",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{2}}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_answer_policy": {
        "version": "revealed-ma-answer-v1",
        "feedback_sha256": "6d7daa5e116342a6661559f7088c2a3cdbeaad880bba5aa567d86fb5bf1f45bb"
      },
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 561,
      "difficulty": "moderate",
