    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-130822",
      "knowledge_point_id": "ecdc6a5a-5aba-5547-97aa-db3cd2e90ae6",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Minor in a NxN Matrix",
      "problem": "What is the minor of ${q}_{22}$ in \n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 19 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "To get the minor of ${q}_{22}$, we remove the $2$nd row and $2$nd column:\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ ∗ & 3 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & ∗ & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{22}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\n$$",
