    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-129040",
      "knowledge_point_id": "11b6d79a-b13d-5e77-899d-8b1b91c872b8",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing Variance Given the Expected Value of a Random Variable and Its Square",
      "problem": "If $\\text{E}[X]=7$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=58,$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =58-{7}^{2} \\\\  & =58-49 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
